Usage: printenv [OPTION]... [VARIABLE]...

Print all or part of environment.

If no VARIABLE is specified, print all environment variables.
If one or more VARIABLE names are specified, print the values of those
variables only.

Options:
  -0, --null    end each output line with NUL, not newline

OPTIONS:
  -0, --null     end each output line with NUL, not newline
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
